  "issue_gist": "PoissonDistributionImpl's constructor PoissonDistributionImpl(double p, NormalDistribution z) calls overridable setters (setNormal, setMean), which is unsafe because a subclass can override them. It also stores the caller-supplied NormalDistribution reference and later mutates it, so the caller's object is modified unexpectedly. The suggested fix is to make the class immutable and create the NormalDistribution internally.",
